    <statement><p>Consider the graph of the function <m>f(x)</m> shown below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap2Sec2__Q15_pg-image-1.png" width="41%">
<shortdescription>a graph of a function with a positive, increasing slope.</shortdescription>
</image>
<p>Using this graph, for each of the following pairs of numbers
decide which is larger.  <em>Be sure that you can explain your
answer.</em></p>
<p><alert>A.</alert>
<m>f(3)</m> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>&lt;</p>
</li><li>
<p>=</p>
</li><li>
<p>&gt;</p>
</li></ul> <m>f(4)</m></p>
<p><alert>B.</alert>
<m>f(3) - f(2)</m> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0002"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>&lt;</p>
</li><li>
<p>=</p>
</li><li>
<p>&gt;</p>
</li></ul> <m>f(2) - f(1)</m></p>
<p><alert>C.</alert>
<m>\frac{f(2) - f(1)}{2 - 1}</m>
  <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0003"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>&lt;</p>
</li><li>
<p>=</p>
</li><li>
<p>&gt;</p>
</li></ul>
  <m>\frac{f(3) - f(1)}{3 - 1}</m></p>
<p><alert>D.</alert>
<m>f'(1)</m> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0004"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>&lt;</p>
</li><li>
<p>=</p>
</li><li>
<p>&gt;</p>
</li></ul> <m>f'(4)</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\verb!&lt;!}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\verb!&gt;!}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\verb!&lt;!}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
