        <m>{\verb!&lt;!}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>A.</alert>
Since <m>f</m> is increasing,
<m>f(3)</m> &lt; <m>f(4)</m>.



<alert>B.</alert>
From the figure, it appears that
<m>f(3) - f(2)</m> &gt;
<m>f(2) - f(1)</m>.



<alert>C.</alert>
The quantity <m>\frac{f(2)-f(1)}{2-1}</m>
represents the slope of the secant line connecting the points on the graph
at <m>x=1</m> and <m>x=2</m>. This is less than the slope of the
secant line connecting the points at <m>x=1</m> and <m>x=3</m>, which
is <m>\frac{f(3)-f(1)}{3-1}</m>



<alert>D.</alert>
The function is less steep at <m>x=1</m> than at <m>x=4</m>, so
<m>f'(1)</m> &lt; <m>f'(4)</m>.



</solution>
